# Client, in `package a; package b`, finds the given a.T of package a.b; package a has another.
> p/compile
# Deleting Outer.scala removes a given from package a, so the classes of package a recompile in a second cycle.
# The first cycle compiles no source, so it never reaches the phase that writes early output with pipelining;
# early output must still be written once, by the last cycle.
$ delete p/Outer.scala
> p/compile
